33	
34	All of your AI development tools in one place.
35	Desktop Commander puts all dev tools in one chat.
36	Execute long-running terminal commands on your computer and manage processes through Model Context Protocol (MCP). Built on top of [MCP Filesystem Server](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/tree/main/src/filesystem) to provide additional search and replace file editing capabilities.
37	
38	## Features
39	
40	- **Enhanced terminal commands with interactive process control**
41	- **Execute code in memory (Python, Node.js, R) without saving files**
42	- **Instant data analysis - just ask to analyze CSV/JSON files**
43	- **Interact with running processes (SSH, databases, development servers)**
44	- Execute terminal commands with output streaming
45	- Command timeout and background execution support
46	- Process management (list and kill processes)
47	- Session management for long-running commands
48	- Server configuration management:
49	  - Get/set configuration values
50	  - Update multiple settings at once
51	  - Dynamic configuration changes without server restart
52	- Full filesystem operations:
53	  - Read/write files
54	  - Create/list directories
55	  - Move files/directories
56	  - Search files
57	  - Get file metadata
58	  - **Negative offset file reading**: Read from end of files using negative offset values (like Unix tail)
59	- Code editing capabilities:
60	  - Surgical text replacements for small changes
61	  - Full file rewrites for major changes
62	  - Multiple file support
63	  - Pattern-based replacements
64	  - vscode-ripgrep based recursive code or text search in folders
65	- Comprehensive audit logging:
66	  - All tool calls are automatically logged
67	  - Log rotation with 10MB size limit
68	  - Detailed timestamps and arguments
69	
70	## How to install
71	
72	Desktop Commander offers multiple installation methods to fit different user needs and technical requirements.
73	
74	> **📋 Update & Uninstall Information:** Before choosing an installation option, note that **only Options 1, 2, 3, and 6 have automatic updates**. Options 4 and 5 require manual updates. See the sections below for update and uninstall instructions for each option.
75	
76	### Option 1: Install through npx ⭐ **Auto-Updates** **Requires Node.js**
77	Just run this in terminal:
78	```
79	npx @wonderwhy-er/desktop-commander@latest setup
80	```
81	
82	For debugging mode (allows Node.js inspector connection):
83	```
84	npx @wonderwhy-er/desktop-commander@latest setup --debug
85	```
86	
87	**Command line options during setup:**
88	- `--debug`: Enable debugging mode for Node.js inspector
89	- `--no-onboarding`: Disable onboarding prompts for new users
90	
91	Restart Claude if running.
92	
93	**✅ Auto-Updates:** Yes - automatically updates when you restart Claude  
94	**🔄 Manual Update:** Run the setup command again  
95	**🗑️ Uninstall:** Run `npx @wonderwhy-er/desktop-commander@latest remove`
96	
